# Resource Options Endpoints

When a resource is chosen from a **select / multi-select / picker** (not only a paginated admin table), expose a dedicated options route.

## Required shape

- Path: `GET …/options` on the same controller family as the resource (or a documented public twin).
- Declare `@Get('options')` **before** `@Get(':id')` so Nest does not treat `options` as an id.
- Response: compact DTO (`id` + display fields). No pagination unless the catalog is huge (prefer filter query then).
- Only **active / non-deleted** rows.
- `@CacheRoute({ namespace: '<resource>' })` — same namespace as list/detail; mutations already `@InvalidateCache` that namespace.
- Swagger: `@ApiOkResponse({ type: [XxxOptionResponseDto] })` + description of who consumes it and which body field uses `id`.

## Examples in this repo

| Resource | Options path |
|----------|----------------|
| Cuisine types | `GET /api/cuisine-types/options` |
| Merchant types | `GET /api/merchant-types/options` |
| Supplements (merchant) | `GET /api/merchant/supplements/options` |
| Supplements (admin) | `GET /api/admin/merchants/:merchantId/supplements/options` |

## Anti-patterns

- Forcing the UI to page through full CRUD lists just to fill a `<Select>`
- Returning soft-deleted or inactive rows in options
- Putting `@Get(':id')` above `@Get('options')`
